## Bug & root cause

File: `/dayjs/src/plugin/weekYear/index.js`

`weekYear()` only handled the "December date that belongs to next week-year" case (`weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11 → year + 1`). It never handled the symmetric "January date that belongs to the **previous** week-year" case, so early-January dates that fall in week 52/53 of the prior year returned the wrong (current) year. This is exactly the ISO-8601 (`yearStart: 4`) situation: 2017-01-01 → week 52, but `weekYear()` returned 2017 instead of 2016; 2016-01-01 → week 53, returned 2016 instead of 2015; 2021-01-01 → week 53, returned 2021 instead of 2020. The `yearStart` option itself was already honored by `weekOfYear`'s `week()` (it reads `this.$locale().yearStart`), so `weekYear` only needed to interpret the resulting week number correctly.

## Exact diff (`src/plugin/weekYear/index.js`, lines 7–13)

```diff
@@ -7,6 +7,9 @@ export default (o, c) => {
     if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
       return year + 1
     }
+    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
+      return year - 1
+    }
     return year
   }
 }
```

No other file was modified (weekOfYear/isoWeek were left untouched; they were already correct). No test file was touched.

